 1 big thing: Top midterm megadonors 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic: The New York Times Massive midterm spending by Silicon Valley reflects a new activism by tech investors and companies who recognize policy will shape their futures:

 Marc Andreessen and Ben Horowitz, co-founders of the iconic venture-capital firm Andreessen Horowitz , top a list of the biggest midterm donors so far, the N.Y. Times' Teddy Schleifer and Matt Zdun report from FEC filings. 

 George and Alex Soros, father and son, are "the only longtime Democratic megadonors" and "still the biggest fish in the Democratic money world, using their super PACs to back left-leaning groups." Graphic: The New York Times Jeff Yass, co-founder of trading and investment giant Susquehanna International Group, and Elon Musk are Nos. 3 and 4 on the list, followed by One Nation, the nonprofit arm of Republicans' Senate Leadership Fund .

 See the top 20 (NYT gift link). 
 
