 2. 👢 Trump&#x27;s first big midterm money move 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Axios Visuals. Photo: Stefani Reynolds/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump's MAGA Inc. super PAC began its long-awaited midterm spending yesterday with a $10 million TV and digital ad campaign for Texas Senate hopeful Ken Paxton.

 Why it matters: Starting in Texas underscores Republicans' urgency to shore up Paxton, 63, who's in an unexpectedly tight race with 37-year-old Democrat James Talarico, Axios' Alex Isenstadt writes. 👀 Republicans haven't lost statewide in Texas in more than three decades. But Talarico has vastly outraised Paxton, whom some Republicans have criticized for running a lackadaisical campaign.

 Talarico raised $68 million through June, compared with $9 million for Paxton. Talarico dominated the airwaves for much of the summer. The Elon Musk-funded America PAC has reported spending $2.4 million to bolster Paxton.

 Share this story . 
 
