 5. 📊 Poll du jour: AI use, worries rising 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic: NBC News New this morning: M ore people are using AI, and more often. But they still don't trust it. Here are top findings from an NBC News Decision Desk online poll of 7,105 adults, powered by SurveyMonkey (margin of error: ±3.3 points): 

 52% of American adults say they use AI tools very often or sometimes, up 6 points from a June 2025 poll . The share that uses AI very often, 23%, increased from 14% last year. But just 18% say they can trust AI-generated information most or almost all of the time. And an overwhelming 70% of adults are more worried than excited about AI. "Worries about AI transcend age, race, education, partisanship and other typical dividing lines," NBC concludes.

