 7. 🔨 Kennedy Center ceiling shock 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photos: The Kennedy Center A section of ceiling in the Kennedy Center's Grand Foyer collapsed around 5 p.m. Friday following stormy weather, an official tells me. 

 Context: The Kennedy Center's Trump-aligned board is fighting in court to add Trump's name to the façade and close the center for two years as it undergoes $250 million in renovations. (AP) Roma Daravi, vice president of P.R., told me: "Another example of the urgent need to close for renovation and revitalization, as our Chairman President Trump has championed. Fortunately, no one was injured when the main hall's ceiling collapsed."

 "This structural failure stems from decades of neglect and deferred maintenance by the previous leadership, and there's no justification for further delays in restoring America's cultural center." Get the latest . 

 
 
