 8. ⏱️ 1 for the road: Remade &quot;60 Minutes&quot; to debut 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Jon Wertheim of "60 Minutes" interviews L.A. Rams head coach Sean McVay. Photo: CBS News A week from tonight, "60 Minutes" will debut its 59th season with "an inside look at the Los Angeles Rams, hailed as a superteam and an early favorite to win the Super Bowl," CBS News announced .

 Why it matters: It's the show's first episode under executive producer Nick Bilton as part of CBS News editor-in-chief Bari Weiss' overhaul that included firing three correspondents. 🏈 Jon Wertheim, the show's sports correspondent, interviewed Rams general manager Les Snead, head coach Sean McVay and veteran quarterback Matthew Stafford, the L.A. Times' Steve Battaglio reports : 

 "The segment will also explore team owner Stan Kroenke's investment in technology, including artificial intelligence, to help the team gain an edge on the field." I'm told the other two segments, to be announced this week, will be hard news stories, possibly including a major newsmaker interview. The "60" season opener follows a Week 1 NFL game. The show "has often turned to sports-related segments when a season premiere follows a late afternoon NFL game," Battaglio points out:

 "This year's premiere should get a strong boost, as most of the country will get CBS coverage of a late afternoon matchup between the Green Bay Packers and the Minnesota Vikings, two contenders in the highly competitive NFC North." Watch a 15-second teaser . 

 
 
